description:
Formal grammar of the table-schema JSON a plugin returns from load_schema. Encoded from OB's parser (src/plugin/v2/external_table/ob_ext_schema_parser.cpp) and type mapper (ob_ext_type_mapper.cpp); a document valid against this schema parses cleanly in OB. Field names correspond to the OB_EXT_K_* constants in ob_external_table_protocol.h.

Rules JSON Schema cannot express (also enforced by OB, hard errors):
  - 'name' values must be unique across top-level columns;
  - 'field_id' values must be unique across top-level columns;
  - 'partition_keys' entries SHOULD name an existing column (an unmatched name is only WARNed and skipped, not an error).
Evolution rule: unknown keys at any level are tolerated (OB logs a loud WARN, never fails) — plugins may add private keys, OB may add new known keys, independently compiled builds keep working.
